# ~/.config/skhd/skhdrc -- installed by tiler/install.sh. It binds nothing
# itself; it only loads the three key files, in this order:
#
#   local.skhd    yours: never shipped, never overwritten (the installers seed
#                 it once from tiler/local.skhd.example, all commented out)
#   tiler.skhd    the tiler's keys (tiler/tiler.skhd)
#   gallery.skhd  the Gallery's keys (skhd/gallery.skhd)
#
# ORDER MATTERS, verified in skhd's source (v0.3.9, parse.c + hashtable.h): the
# .load files are parsed in the order written here, and a hotkey defined twice
# is neither an error nor a warning -- the FIRST definition wins and the later
# one is dropped silently. Loading local.skhd first therefore lets it replace
# any shipped binding and add new ones. skhd has no unbind: to disable a
# shipped key, bind it in local.skhd to a no-op (`: true`).
#
# A missing .load file is only a warning in skhd's err log, but a file that did
# not exist when skhd started is not hotloaded until `skhd --reload`; hence the
# installers create local.skhd (and an empty gallery.skhd placeholder) up front.
.load "local.skhd"
.load "tiler.skhd"
.load "gallery.skhd"
